  "player_text": "I stay on the main road and ask the first local I pass where a traveler can get a bed and a meal before curfew.",
  "visible_motivation": "I'm inside the gate district with the curfew still in force, and the town is ahead of me.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want a named place to sleep tonight so I'm off the street before dusk.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "\"A tavern runner, wiping rain from their brow as they ward off the drizzle near a steaming barrel of stew, glances up when you approach. \"If you're a traveler looking for shelter and a meal before curfew,\" they say, voice low and hurried, \"the Rusty Tankard down the road is your best bet. They offer beds and a hot meal, but you'll want to get in before sundown.\" They gesture down the main road where a weathered sign points toward the tavern's murky lantern-lit entrance. \"After that, the curfew tightens and the gates shut. It's not wise to be caught outside.\"",
